#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1150 expect=violation domain=TI
#note "DISCRIMINATING - the OPPOSITE half of valid_blank_tivers. NO TIVERS COLUMN AT ALL: TIVERS is Permissible and a grouping key absent from the dataset is silently DROPPED and the check REGROUPS on what remains, so the rule behaves exactly like FDA-SD1150 and fires on the tie. TIVERS is in Output_Variables but absent from the data, so it is omitted from the value map - DO NOT PIN IT."
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 IETESTCD=INCL01 IETEST="Age 18 years or older"
#expectViolationAt row=2 IETESTCD=INCL01 IETEST="Age at least 18 years"
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TI
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col IETESTCD type=Char
col IETEST   type=Char
---
S1 | TI | INCL01 | Age 18 years or older
S1 | TI | INCL01 | Age at least 18 years
